{"candidates":[{"content":"The preference for corroborated theories (SRC_001) inherits its normative force from an evolutionary selection mechanism (SRC_003); the 'decision' to prefer is not a voluntary convention but a methodological trait that survived because it correlates with truth-likeness. REFUTED IF: The history of science shows that methodological rules promoting corroboration have frequently led to the retention of false theories while eliminating true ones (i.e., if the selection pressure is orthogonal to verisimilitude).","evidence_refs":[{"block":"ff007a913aed","quote":"program:lineage_ref"}],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"03f8b3f2f0045799db01bdb5c40524ddb0adf4dcd784fe98187408e4f273c86b"},{"role":"dependence","target":"9f4b6c4e088cd97b6be95d65128df768599424916141496d8b4eadcfd54ae935"}],"typicality":0.85},{"content":"The 'decision postulate' in SRC_004 contradicts the 'evolutionary selection' in SRC_003 regarding the source of rationality: one posits a voluntary, internal convention, while the other posits an external, adaptive necessity. They are incompatible unless the 'decision' is merely the conscious awareness of an unconscious evolutionary imperative. REFUTED IF: It can be demonstrated that scientists can and do voluntarily adopt methodological rules that are maladaptive or counter-evolutionary without losing their status as rational agents.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"459e3f4e6098c090a0c99c13070152da30cd3c5e88dee54d561167281a3b5234"},{"role":"dependence","target":"9f4b6c4e088cd97b6be95d65128df768599424916141496d8b4eadcfd54ae935"}],"typicality":0.65},{"content":"SRC_002's claim that rationality is 'internal to the game of science' reduces to SRC_005's 'procedural convention' only if the 'game' itself is static; however, if the game evolves (as per SRC_003), the dependence shifts: the convention depends on the survival of the game, not vice versa. REFUTED IF: The rules of scientific procedure (the 'game') remain constant across paradigm shifts, implying the game does not evolve but only its content does.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"5da47459bf8faba2d74749bbbd0e17b17438d162198e6ddc899717f6aeb17e55"},{"role":"dependence","target":"48969427b03779fe5b60e6d65e7ca0dd60ef43fd032d937aa00bf30552f8d043"},{"role":"dependence","target":"9f4b6c4e088cd97b6be95d65128df768599424916141496d8b4eadcfd54ae935"}],"typicality":0.45},{"content":"The 'convention' described in SRC_001 abstracts the specific causal mechanisms of SRC_003 into a normative rule, losing the explanatory power regarding why this specific convention was selected over others. REFUTED IF: The specific content of the convention (preferring corroboration) can be derived purely from logical consistency requirements without any reference to evolutionary survival or historical success.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"03f8b3f2f0045799db01bdb5c40524ddb0adf4dcd784fe98187408e4f273c86b"},{"role":"dependence","target":"9f4b6c4e088cd97b6be95d65128df768599424916141496d8b4eadcfd54ae935"}],"typicality":0.3},{"content":"SRC_005 and SRC_004 share a mechanism of 'voluntarism' where the agent bridges the is-ought gap by fiat, but this mechanism integrates poorly with SRC_003's determinism unless the 'volition' is an illusion generated by successful adaptation. REFUTED IF: Agents possess genuine libertarian free will capable of choosing methodological rules that defy evolutionary pressures while maintaining coherence.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"48969427b03779fe5b60e6d65e7ca0dd60ef43fd032d937aa00bf30552f8d043"},{"role":"dependence","target":"459e3f4e6098c090a0c99c13070152da30cd3c5e88dee54d561167281a3b5234"},{"role":"dependence","target":"9f4b6c4e088cd97b6be95d65128df768599424916141496d8b4eadcfd54ae935"}],"typicality":0.55},{"content":"The 'relativism' feared in SRC_002 is the necessary consequence of accepting SRC_003's evolutionary view without a teleological guarantee; if selection does not aim at truth, then the 'surviving' methodology is just one of many possible adaptive strategies, making SRC_002's 'internal rationality' relative to the specific environment. REFUTED IF: There exists a unique, universally optimal methodological rule for all possible environments, rendering the evolutionary contingency irrelevant.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"5da47459bf8faba2d74749bbbd0e17b17438d162198e6ddc899717f6aeb17e55"},{"role":"dependence","target":"9f4b6c4e088cd97b6be95d65128df768599424916141496d8b4eadcfd54ae935"}],"typicality":0.2}],"simulation_proposals":[]}